{
    "attributes": {
        "action": "Review the balance between religious freedoms & equality laws to protect rights",
        "additional_details": "Everyone must be free to practise, change or leave a religion, or criticise its beliefs and practices, without intimidation, discrimination or coercion. \r\n\r\nReligious freedom must be balanced with equality before the law and individual rights. No religious doctrine should justify undermining another person\u2019s autonomy, dignity or legal protections. \r\n\r\nWe urge the Government to identify gaps in the law, consider further measures and provide preventative safeguards against religiously justified discrimination, coercion and psychological harm, particularly for women, LGBT people and former believers. \r\n\r\nEveryone\u2019s rights and freedoms must be protected equally, whether they hold religious beliefs or not.",
        "background": "We call on the Government to review protections and introduce safeguards so religious beliefs, practices or institutions cannot justify coercion, discrimination or interference with others\u2019 fundamental rights and freedoms.",
